{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"componentIndex","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentIndex"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","externalID":"s:12FirebladeECS9ComponentPAAE14componentIndexSivpZ","extendedModule":"FirebladeECS","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dense index of this component type."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentIndex"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storages address their per-type state and the per-entity component bitset by this value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default implementation assigns indices lazily: the first access of a type takes the next free index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the process, later accesses look it up in a thread-safe table. The index is process-wide, not per ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so all nexuses of a process agree on it. Indices are dense (","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types used so far) and unbounded.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They depend on the order of first use and are not stable between process launches;","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/RegistrableComponent\/stableIdentifier","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for persistent data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift has no stored static properties in generic types, so a plain conformance can not cache its index in a static."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Provide your own implementation (the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component"},{"type":"text","text":" macro will) as a stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static let"},{"type":"text","text":" for a plain load,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but only if you can guarantee that two types never share an index and that it is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< 1_048_576","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Indices are process-wide: a hand-assigned index must not collide with a lazily assigned one of another type.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A collision or an index out of range traps at first use of the type in a nexus."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(1)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/component\/componentindex-5oxlf"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Component"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Component\/componentIndex-5oxlf","interfaceLanguage":"s